---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Counterfact — Build the frontend. Don’t wait for the backend."
  description="Turn an OpenAPI document into a useful local API in one command, then add custom behavior only when your frontend needs it."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="page-shell header-content">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Counterfact home">
        <img src="/counterfact.svg" alt="" width="180" height="31" />
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#quick-start">Quick start</a>
        <a href="/docs/getting-started" data-analytics-event="getting_started_opened">Docs</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/counterfact/api-simulator" data-analytics-event="github_opened">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero page-shell" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Local APIs from OpenAPI</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Build the frontend. Don’t wait for the backend.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Counterfact turns an OpenAPI document into a useful local API in one command.
        Point your frontend at localhost and start building against generated responses
        before the real backend is ready.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#quick-start" data-analytics-event="quickstart_opened">Try it now</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/getting-started" data-analytics-event="getting_started_opened">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-shell command-section" aria-labelledby="command-heading">
      <h2 id="command-heading">Start with your OpenAPI document</h2>
      <div class="command-panel">
        <code id="install-cmd">npx counterfact@latest https://petstore3.swagger.io/api/v3/openapi.json api</code>
        <button id="copy-btn" class="copy-button" type="button" aria-label="Copy command" data-analytics-event="quickstart_command_copied">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <p class="supporting-text">
        Requires Node.js 22+. For a repeatable project or CI workflow,
        <a href="/docs/first-10-minutes#install-a-pinned-version">install a pinned version</a>
        and commit the lockfile.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-shell workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The development loop</p>
      <h2 id="workflow-heading">Start generated. Make only the behavior your screen needs.</h2>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div>
          <p>
            Counterfact generates editable, typed route handlers from the contract.
            Change one response, save the file, and refresh the frontend. The server
            hot-reloads the handler without throwing away your in-memory state.
          </p>
          <ol class="compact-steps">
            <li>Make the first browser request.</li>
            <li>Shape one response for the current screen.</li>
            <li>Add a small create/read workflow when state matters.</li>
            <li>Exercise one loading, empty, or failure state.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <pre><code>// api/routes/pet/&#123;petId&#125;.ts
export const GET: HTTP_GET = ($) =&gt;
  $.response[200].json(&#123;
    id: $.path.petId,
    name: "Fluffy",
    status: "available"
  &#125;);</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-shell examples-section" aria-labelledby="examples-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Use it in a real workflow</p>
      <h2 id="examples-heading">Two runnable paths beyond Petstore</h2>
      <div class="example-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>React and Vite</h3>
          <p>Build a profile screen against a local API while the production endpoint is still unavailable.</p>
          <a href="/docs/examples/react-vite" data-analytics-event="ecosystem_example_opened" data-analytics-example="react-vite">Run the React example</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Playwright error states</h3>
          <p>Verify success, not-found, and temporary-failure UI states through a real HTTP boundary.</p>
          <a href="/docs/examples/playwright-error-states" data-analytics-event="ecosystem_example_opened" data-analytics-example="playwright">Run the Playwright example</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="quick-start" class="page-shell quick-start" aria-labelledby="quick-start-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Quick start</p>
      <h2 id="quick-start-heading">A useful API before you write a handler</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <h3>Run the command</h3>
          <p>Counterfact reads the document, writes editable routes and generated types, then starts a server.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Point the frontend at localhost</h3>
          <p>The base URL is <code>http://localhost:3100</code>. A browser app can make an ordinary request:</p>
          <pre><code>const response = await fetch("http://localhost:3100/pet/1");
const pet = await response.json();</code></pre>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Get a generated response</h3>
          <p>Supported operations return schema-derived sample data immediately. For example:</p>
          <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": 1,
  "name": "string",
  "status": "available"
&#125;</code></pre>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="supporting-text">
        The defaults are a useful starting point for frontend work and exploration—not a claim that your backend behavior is complete.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-shell more-section" aria-labelledby="more-heading">
      <h2 id="more-heading">When your frontend needs more</h2>
      <p>
        Replace a generated response with a custom handler when a screen needs a specific case.
        Add only the state, failures, latency, proxying, or tests that the workflow needs.
      </p>
      <div class="link-list" aria-label="Advanced Counterfact guides">
        <a href="/docs/features/routes">Custom responses</a>
        <a href="/docs/features/state">State</a>
        <a href="/docs/patterns/simulate-failures">Failures and latency</a>
        <a href="/docs/features/proxy">Proxying</a>
        <a href="/docs/patterns/automated-integration-tests">Tests</a>
        <a href="/docs/features/repl">REPL</a>
        <a href="/docs/comparison" data-analytics-event="comparison_opened">Compare tools</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="page-shell footer-content">
      <span>Counterfact</span>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" data-analytics-event="getting_started_opened">Getting started</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/counterfact/api-simulator" data-analytics-event="github_opened">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</MainLayout>
